---
import InfoCard from '../ui/InfoCard';
import StatCard from '../ui/StatCard';
---
<section id="evidence" class="bg-surface/50 py-16 md:py-20"><div class="report-container"><div class="mb-10"><p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-brand-text">Evidence and decisions</p><h2 class="text-3xl text-ink md:text-4xl">The useful part is what failed</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-ink-muted">The first prototype established feasibility but made the real problem visible: hardware can measure a desk, but it cannot create a habit by itself.</p></div><div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3"><InfoCard tone="success" title="Worked" items={['Desk height measurement via a laser sensor.', 'Basic telemetry and a controllable prototype.', 'A real signal that can feed the decision loop.']} /><InfoCard tone="danger" title="Failed" items={['The plexi enclosure overheated electronics.', 'Relays and presence sensing were unreliable.', 'The controller was built but never finished or integrated.']} /><InfoCard tone="learn" title="Learned" items={['The computer should own the UX loop.', 'A smaller sensor is easier to test and replace.', 'The current question is behaviour, not a hardware moat.']} /></div><div class="mt-5 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2"><StatCard label="W1 cost (sourced)" value="~700 PLN / 200 USD" /><StatCard label="Measured standing time" value="~8% in a small sample with nudging" /></div></div></section>
